# Conversion specifiers that the spec's list does not have, and a % that ends the format: what they mean is
# not defined. macOS and GNU date give them a meaning (%s seconds since the Epoch, %z numeric zone, %N
# nanoseconds, %k blank-padded hour, %-d without padding, a lone % as a % ...). Ours refuses them, nothing is
# written, like it refuses sleep 1.5: this project does not take extensions.
+%Q
+%
+%E
+%Ea
+%Oc
+%-d
+%s
+%z
+%N
+%k
